00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:44.240
Okay. Yeah, I think I would, I think I would consider it like, like if you wanted the log line for this, like think, um, Mega Man meets that helicopter flash game.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.160
That's the log line.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.520
Okay. That's, that's not terrible.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:55.940
I, I think that, yeah, this is definitely more a puzzler than anything else.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:11.640
And I know that like in the Wikipedia entry and, and Mike just said it, uh, he said shmup and I'm like, yeah, there's a lot of stuff thrown around and you shoot like you would a shmup, but like there's too much weird.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:21.260
Yeah. Claustrophobic navigation and almost lock and key like interaction with the environment that I can't call this a shmup.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:31.420
Yeah. I think, I think navigation pit plays so much more of a role in this like precise navigation, uh, more of a role in this than like a shmup would.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:37.720
A shmup is about like fast, like moving fast and taking out anything in your way and avoiding hits.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:42.920
This is like about figuring out where to go and like doing it in a technical way.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.260
There's no flow.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.520
Uh, it's very, you're going to be playing this very methodically.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.340
Right. Uh, it kind of reminds me of air fortress.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:04:09.640
Um, that, that game obviously had like a much clearer objective in each stage and, and, um, you know, maybe not, uh, maybe not so puzzly, but it reminds me of that in the way that like you're inside a, uh, you're inside of a space air.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:14.940
Uh, yeah, you're like in the, it's like a giant space station, but yeah, space station.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:30.980
Right. And you're a ship inside of that trying to just basically, uh, take down enemies, not in the sense of to progress that just to kind of clear off the area in front of you to then solve, uh, you know, we're saying the heist portion of it.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:31.960
Like, right. Yeah.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:37.300
We keep saying puzzles, but it's more like, uh, the puzzles are in the timing, right?

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.700
It's more precision based than anything else.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:56.120
I guess the only thing that's making me say puzzle in this is that, so, all right, you're, you're kind of going through a labyrinth and the schmuck portion is you have a never ending series of tiny what's it's coming at you.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:16.900
They have to shoot or avoid, but the, the puzzling more so is there's going to be other non moving hazards, um, that you have, you have several different kinds of attack and these like non moving hazards are only susceptible to one of those.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:24.100
Like there's your bombs and like the, anything that's like circular is fine with bombs.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:35.180
And then there's the green, uh, and you can just shoot at those, but in anything that like you can't get like a horizontal edge on, you're going to have to use your bouncer buddies.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:40.240
