Uh, which, what is your favorite music track in this?

00:28:38.960 --> 00:28:44.440
Uh, is it the one that goes, boom, boom, boom, over and over and over again?

00:28:44.560 --> 00:28:46.160
Or is it the one that's a music track?

00:28:47.200 --> 00:28:49.140
Oh, I like the music probably better.

00:28:49.280 --> 00:28:52.420
Me too. Joe, you don't know how lucky these people are, okay?

00:28:52.680 --> 00:28:54.960
The ZX Spectrum one didn't have music.

00:28:55.080 --> 00:28:55.940
I would take that.

00:28:56.180 --> 00:28:58.540
So this is a major upgrade.

00:28:59.200 --> 00:29:03.580
Because, I mean, unless I'm, uh, did something wrong here.

00:29:03.580 --> 00:29:15.340
You start the game, and the whole time, when it's paused, when it's not paused, when you're shooting, when anything's happening, nothing makes any noise, and it just goes, boom, boom, boom, constantly.

00:29:16.680 --> 00:29:22.380
Then, halfway through the game, I realize you can pause it and press B, and then a music track will play instead.

00:29:22.980 --> 00:29:25.700
Okay, alright, this is the difference here.

00:29:25.700 --> 00:29:35.400
Now, there is a hi-fi version that just does away with music, this is via the manual, for, like, higher fidelity sounds.

00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:41.000
And then there is a music version with, you know, bleeps and bloops, I imagine.

00:29:41.100 --> 00:29:42.720
But I don't think I ever changed it.

00:29:43.220 --> 00:29:46.200
Uh, so, I guess you found the button.

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:50.220
So, is the wooing one, the whooshing, whatever you call it?

00:29:50.240 --> 00:29:51.080
That's hi-fi. That's hi-fi?

00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:56.160
I don't remember there even being, like, much sound, other than that, that...

00:29:56.160 --> 00:29:58.700
I'm sure there's, like, sounds for explosions.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:08.940
Like, I'm not... We could fight about the music and audio all day, but I think everybody thinks it's about time for the Essential Games List.

